"2048 for B8Script. Slide the tiles with w a s d: two tiles with the same number";
"merge into one. Make a 2048 tile, and keep going if you like. q quits.";
"Only the left slide is written: for the others the board is turned clockwise";
"(s once, d twice, w three times), slid left and turned on round to the start.";
"A tile is kept as its exponent in a byte (1 is 2, 11 is 2048), and its value";
"is worked out only to print it, in two cells, so no tile overflows a cell.";

"Variables";
"  b  the board, 16 bytes, cell = row*4+column, each 0 (empty) or an exponent";
"  c  the board as it is on the screen, so also as it was before a move";
"  t  scratch board for turning";
"  s h  score: h*10000+s   x y  a value: x*10000+y   g  a 2048 was made";
"  w  the 2048 message has been shown   q  no moves left   k  turns   e l v z m";
"  n  key   a i j  scratch   r  random state";

"Routines";
[M/%;]
[R r@75*74+:r! 256/;255& %M]
[K0 1(;r@1+r!1?:0=)]
[L13'10']

"Screen. C: clear   Y: row column -- move the cursor   E: clear to the end of the line";
[C"/[[2J/[[H"$]
[Y27'91'%#59'#72']
[E"/[[K"$]

"P: e -- set x,y to 2 to the power e, as x*10000+y";
[P 0x! 1y! 1( :1<\ y@:+y! x@:+x! y@9999>( y@10000-y! x@1+x! 0) 1- 1);]

"D: n -- how many digits n has (n is 0 to 32767)";
[D z! 1 z@9>- z@99>- z@999>- z@9999>-]

"H: print the value x,y";
[H x@( x@# y@:1000<("0"$0):100<("0"$0):10<("0"$0)# 0) x@0=( y@# 0)]

"B: n -- print n spaces";
[B 1( :1<\ 32' 1- 1);]

"T: e -- print the tile with exponent e, 7 characters wide, centred";
[T e! e@0=:( 7B 0)\ e@P x@( x@D4+ 0) x@0=( y@D 0) l! 7l@- 2/; :B H 7l@-%-B]

"Q: i -- move the cursor to the middle line of cell i";
[Q 4/ 8*4+ % 4*6+ % Y]

"F: draw the empty frame";
[F 0j! 1( j@4+ 3Y j@4M( "|       |       |       |       |"$ 0)
   j@4M0=( "+-------+-------+-------+-------+"$ 0) j@1+:j! 17<)]

"V: draw every cell that differs from c, and make c the board";
[V 0i! 1( i@b@+, i@c@+, =0=( i@Q i@b@+,T i@b@+, i@c@+. 0) i@1+:i! 16<)]

"A: the score";
[A 22 3Y "Score "$ s@y! h@x! H E]

"Z: e -- add 2 to the power e to the score";
[Z P s@y@+s! h@x@+h! s@9999>( s@10000-s! h@1+h! 0)]

"O: turn the board clockwise";
[O 0i! 1( i@4/ 3%- 4*+ b@+, i@t@+. i@1+:i! 16<)
   0i! 1( i@t@+, i@b@+. i@1+:i! 16<)]

"S: slide every row left, merging equal pairs once. k is where the next tile goes,";
"   l the last tile placed while it may still merge";
[S 0j! 1( j@4*b@+a! 0k! 0l! 0i! 1( a@i@+,v!
      v@( v@l@=:( v@1+ :a@k@+1-. :Z 11=( 1g! 0) 0l! 0)0=( v@a@k@+. k@1+k! v@l! 0) 0)
      i@1+:i! 4<)
   1( k@4<0=\ 0a@k@+. k@1+k! 1) j@1+:j! 4<)]

"G: k -- slide toward one side: turn k times, slide left, turn back";
[G :{ 1( :1<\ O 1- 1); S } 4%- 3& 1( :1<\ O 1- 1);]

"X: -- flag  has the board changed from c?";
[X 0 0i! 1( i@b@+, i@c@+, =0= | i@1+:i! 16<)]

"U: -- flag  can any move change the board? (an empty cell, or two equal neighbours)";
[U 0z! 0i! 1( i@b@+,v! v@0=( 1z! 0) i@3&3<( i@1+b@+,v@=( 1z! 0) 0)
   i@12<( i@4+b@+,v@=( 1z! 0) 0) i@1+:i! 16<) z@]

"N: a new tile in a random empty cell: a 2, or one time in ten a 4";
[N 0m! 0i! 1( i@b@+,0=( m@1+m! 0) i@1+:i! 16<) m@R m!
   0i! 1( i@b@+,0=( m@0=( 1 10R0=- i@b@+. 0) m@1-m! 0) i@1+:i! 16<)]

"Main program";
16_b! 16_c! 16_t! 0r!
C "2048"$ L L "Slide the tiles with w a s d. Two tiles with the same number merge into one."$ L
"Make a 2048 tile. q quits."$ L L "Press a key."$ K;
1( 0i! 1( 0i@b@+. 255i@c@+. i@1+:i! 16<) 0s! 0h! 0g! 0w! 0q! N N
   C 2 3Y "2048     w a s d slide   q quits"$ F V A
   1( 23 3Y 0? 32| n! -1k! 0i! 1( "asdw"i@+, n@=( i@k! 0) i@1+:i! 4<)
      k@-1>( k@G X( N V A 0) 0)
      g@ w@0= &( 23 3Y "You made 2048! Keep going if you like."$ 1w! 0)
      U0=( 1q! 0)
   q@0= n@113=0= &)
   23 3Y q@( "No more moves. "$ 0) "Score "$ s@y! h@x! H ". Play again? (y//n) "$ E
   K 121=)
L "Bye."$ L
